---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="Privacy Policy — Pulse"
  description="Pulse Privacy Policy: Local-first architecture, zero telemetry, zero analytical tracking, direct peer-to-peer TLS communication."
>
  <div class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <h1 class="page-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="page-subtitle">Effective Date: September 13, 2026 • Version 1.0</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="container">
    <div class="legal-container">
      <div class="legal-highlight">
        <p><strong>The short version:</strong> Pulse does not collect, store, transmit, or monetize your personal data. All monitoring traffic travels directly between your Mac and your Linux hosts over encrypted connections. We operate zero cloud relays and collect zero telemetry.</p>
      </div>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>1. Zero Telemetry & Analytics</h2>
        <p>Pulse (both the macOS application and the Linux agent daemon) contains no tracking code, telemetry SDKs, Google Analytics, Mixpanel, Crashlytics, or third-party analytical beacons. We do not track your IP address, device identifier, hardware configuration, server count, or usage habits.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>2. Direct Point-to-Point Architecture</h2>
        <p>Pulse does not operate a hosted SaaS backend or cloud proxy server. All communications occur strictly point-to-point:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Direct IP / LAN:</strong> Encrypted WebSocket and TLS 1.3 directly between your Mac and your server's listening port.</li>
          <li><strong>Tailscale:</strong> End-to-end WireGuard tunnel between devices on your private Tailnet.</li>
          <li><strong>Cloudflare Tunnel:</strong> Direct tunnel through Cloudflare edge using your own Cloudflare account credentials.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Your server metrics, system logs, Docker container names, and systemd units remain exclusively on your devices.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>3. Local Storage of Credentials</h2>
        <p>All sensitive configuration data is retained locally on your machines:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Server authentication tokens, TLS fingerprints (TOFU pinning), and host addresses are saved in your macOS user profile and application storage.</li>
          <li>On the Linux node, configuration and generated TLS certificates are stored in <code>/etc/pulse-agent</code> (root mode) or <code>~/.pulse</code> (user mode) with strict <code>0600</code> file permissions.</li>
          <li>Pairing codes (<code>XXX-XXX</code>) are ephemeral with a 10-minute time-to-live and are deleted immediately upon successful pairing or expiration.</li>
          <li>Tokens copied to your clipboard are purged automatically from memory after 60 seconds.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>4. External Integrations (Optional)</h2>
        <p>If you enable optional third-party integrations:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Telegram Bot Notifications:</strong> Outbound alert webhooks connect directly from your Linux agent to the official Telegram Bot API (<code>api.telegram.org</code>) using your own Bot Token. No intermediary server is involved.</li>
          <li><strong>Software Updates:</strong> The macOS app uses Sparkle 2 to check for updates by fetching the static <code>appcast.xml</code> manifest from GitHub Releases. No identifiers are sent during update checks.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>5. Open Source Verification</h2>
        <p>Both the macOS client and Linux agent are open source under the MIT License. You are welcome to audit the source code, compile from source, or monitor outgoing network connections via tools like Little Snitch or Wireshark to verify compliance with this policy.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>6. Contact</h2>
        <p>If you have any questions regarding privacy or security practices, open an issue or discussion on the official GitHub repository at <a href="https://github.com/miftahganzz/Pulse" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--accent);">github.com/miftahganzz/Pulse</a>.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
